														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2824247">
									

<p>Of all the narrative possibilities of a picture frame that makes pictures come to life, &quot;and then they attack&quot; is the least interesting. There are some other issues: the testing log goes on too long, the note about replacing the irresponsible doctor is bizarre when the next supervisor takes an even bigger risk, and there are odd phrasing choices (eg &quot;my niece Harry&quot; - ?). But the decision to makes this a picture frame that kills you is the one that is fatal to any possibility of interest, and the window dressing of backstory isn't enough to redeem it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
