					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="2826145"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1495034808 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 May 2017 15:26</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2824266">
									

<p>I'd take objection to the idea that it's just &quot;and then they attack&quot;. The whole point is that the frame can only portray a distorted image, because it's a channel for the creator's grief over Elijah's death, but without a picture of Elijah it doesn't know what to do. So it just creates versions of the painting through the prism of a grief it can't understand, because it doesn't know what it's grieving for; they end up being emotionally disturbed or somehow distorted from the paintings' meaning. If that makes sense.</p>
<p>Though, looking at it again, they are all a bit more violent than I'd initially intended&#8230; might change that at some point.</p>
<p>Otherwise, fair enough. Sorry you didn't like it :).</p>

							</div>

								
					
